#: input/pagecontent/index.md:3
msgid "A traveller's journey"
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/index.md:8
msgid "Before the journey, in the prologue, Onesa and Taifafeki join the WHO Global Digital Health Certification Network (GDHCN): each onboards its Public Key Infrastructure, and through the GDHCN trust list each trusts the other's public keys. Then Sefa, a traveller from Onesa, carries a verifiable International Patient Summary (IPS) signed in Onesa, falls ill in Taifafeki, and shares it at a clinic, which checks the signature with Onesa's key from the GDHCN and gives care."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/index.md:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Every person in this story, and both countries, are fictional. Sefa comes from Onesa (code {code0}) and travels in Taifafeki (code {code1}): two fictional countries shared with the <a0>SMART Trust demo</a0> and the <a1>SMART IPS Pilgrimage guide</a1>. Their codes are ISO 3166-1 user-assigned codes, so they never name a real country."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/index.md:13
msgid "Under each picture, the boxes are this guide's ArchiMate elements: the lit ones are active in that moment, the grey ones are not, and each opens its element. Click a picture to walk through that moment in the <a0>journeys viewer</a0>, or see the whole journey as <a1>ArchiMate</a1>. The boxes are cases of the figure below: Onesa is its Country A, Taifafeki its Country B, and the GDHCN trust list is its trust anchor's list of verified keys."
msgstr ""
